{"availability":"available","full":"nivas/vue-hotel-datepicker","name":"vue-hotel-datepicker","description":"A Vue.js date range picker component without other dependencies for hotels and multi-purpose.","category":"Other","language":"Vue","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2022-12-21T15:23:06Z","updated":"2026-10-07T20:49:31Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://northwalker.github.io/vue-hotel-datepicker/","topics":[],"demo":"https://nivas.github.io/vue-hotel-datepicker/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:31:32.172Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T23:31:32.172Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T23:31:32.172Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T23:31:32.172Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A pure Vue 3 date range picker component without any other dependencies, for hotel date range selection and multi-purpose. It provides date range selecting, minimum and maximum night limitation, disabled dates with selectable check-out days, custom date formatting and localization support. It ships as an inline picker (VueHotelDatepicker) and as a modal (VueHotelDatepickerModal).","The props, events and CSS selectors of 2.3.x are all kept in 3.x, so moving a Vue 2 project to Vue 3 does not require template or CSS changes for this component. 3.1 adds day prices, a legend and half days, and changes two defaults: clicking a free day behind a disabled date and the look of message. See the changelog.","Made and maintained by NIVAS, the digital agency behind the booking sites this datepicker runs on. It started as a fork of northwalker/vue-hotel-datepicker (archived, Vue 2 only)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nivas/vue-hotel-datepicker/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"7bd5f0c6a9ed2cd884d88d6c6ba9b59dfcfa81e87218ed0c3c40a349315ee5ae","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T23:31:32.273Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:31:32.273Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"tex